e top Republican  on the Intelligence Committee Devin  newness  the calls dating back to the spring  raised questions about new NASA's role  in US policy in Ukraine the president  slammed the inquiry from London  publicans argued the report doesn't meet  the Democrats own bar for impeachment  there is nothing compelling there's  nothing overwhelming and the only  bipartisan we have vote we have had in  this house is not to move forward with  impeachment inquiry today for legal  experts will give their view CBS News  legal analyst Jonathan Turley is the  only witness selected by Republicans  he's expected to tell lawmakers in his  opening statement that it is possible  that a case for impeachment could be  made but it cannot be made on this  record  he explained that argument on CBS this  morning  last monitor all this thing is too  narrow it is it doesn't have a broad  foundation and it's an undeveloped  record back in 1998 at a similar hearing  Turley argued that the allegations  against President Clinton went to the  very heart of the legitimacy of his  office and did merit impeachment by the  house you can expect Anthony that some  of the other witnesses will make a  similar case against President Trump  today Nancy thank you we will bring you  the first House Judiciary Committee  hearing on impeachment in the CBS News  special report Norah O'Donnell will  anchor from Washington it begins at  10:00 a.m. 9:00 central and you can find  continuous coverage on our streaming  network cbsn
 

